148
00:12:42,910 --> 00:12:45,850
 Could you use a name to tell customers apart?

149
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:49,170
 Answer is no, like Sven said here.

150
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,340
 Because two people can have the same name.

151
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:56,320
 There might be two Anna Lindqvist here, for example.

152
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:00,930
 So every table has a primary key.

153
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:08,690
 It's a column where every row has a different value, like a personal number.

154
00:13:09,970 --> 00:13:15,620
 So in our table, I mean, in our table, it's customer ID.

155
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:22,370
